IMPORTANT NOTE

    SMB permissions and NTFS permissions are separate authorization
    layers for network access.

    Effective SMB access is constrained by both:

        SMB Share Permissions
                 +
        NTFS Permissions

    The incident demonstrated that correct NTFS permissions alone
    are insufficient to guarantee the expected network access.


INCIDENT

    INC-004 — SMB Share Permissions Prevented Expected Write Access

    Status:
        RESOLVED

    Root Cause:
        SMB shares were created with:

            Everyone -> Read

        while the underlying NTFS ACLs granted:

            ENGINEERING\GG-IT -> Full Control

    Resolution:
        SMB share permissions were updated to allow Full access.

    Verification:
        john.smith successfully created test files on all
        three departmental shares.


